## 📅 INSTALL CRON JOB - OPTION 2: Manual File Placement

If `crontab -e` doesn't work, create a dedicated crontab file:

```bash
# Create user-side crontab directory if it doesn't exist
mkdir -p ~/.crontab.d/

# Copy cron job to dedicated location
cp $HOME/.hermes/gematria/cron/overnight_research.sh ~/.crontab.d/overnight_research.cron

# Add entry to the file:
echo "0 2 * * * cd $HOME/.hermes/gematria && $HOME/.hermes/gematria/cron/overnight_research.sh >> $HOME/.hermes/gematria/logs/overnight_cron.log 2>&1" >> ~/.crontab.d/overnight_research.cron
```

Then source your crontab:

```bash
# Add these lines to your personal crontab file (~/ .crontab) or run:
crontab -l 2>/dev/null | grep -v "^\s*$" > ~/new_crontab.tmp
cat ~/.crontab.d/overnight_research.cron >> ~/new_crontab.tmp
mv ~/new_crontab.tmp ~/.crontab
```

